  "notes": "Issue #603. EXP-514 (Issue #514, ARCHIVE, already merged to main) added a single pooled kidney group (VHL, MTOR, TSC1, TSC2, PTEN, MET, FH) and a single pooled glioma group (IDH1, IDH2, ATRX, TP53, NF1, PTEN, EGFR) as mutated/LOF gene-count burden columns on top of EXP-374. It improved KIRC (+0.0278) and LGG (+0.0172) but GBMLGG (-0.0167) offset the gain, leaving the OOF Macro F1 improvement (+0.0001756) below the +0.001 gate. Direct data/raw/train.csv verification of per-class mutation rates found that both pooled groups mixed genes with opposite class-favoring direction: in glioma, IDH1/IDH2/ATRX/TP53 favor LGG while NF1/PTEN/EGFR favor GBMLGG; in kidney, VHL/MTOR favor KIRC while TSC1/TSC2/MET favor KIPAN, and FH is zero-variance (0 mutated samples in both KIPAN and KIRC) so it carries no information. This matches independent literature (WHO CNS5 IDH-mutant astrocytoma vs IDH-wildtype GBM molecular classification; WHO renal tumor classification's VHL-ccRCC/KIRC and MET-papillary-RCC driver associations) rather than being mined from SUBCLASS. This experiment re-splits the same 14-gene literature panel (minus zero-variance FH, minus noise-level kidney-context PTEN) into four directionally consistent groups instead of two pooled groups (kirc_lineage: VHL, MTOR; kipan_nonccrcc_lineage: TSC1, TSC2, MET; lgg_idh_lineage: IDH1, IDH2, ATRX, TP53; gbm_idh_wildtype_lineage: NF1, PTEN, EGFR), producing 8 burden columns (4 groups x mutated/LOF gene count) instead of EXP-514's 4. EXP-514's own 4 columns are NOT reused in this experiment; this is a fresh ablation against EXP-374, not a stack of EXP-514 on top of EXP-374. EXP-374's stop-notation parser, hotspot-34, Ensembl residue-position isoform mask, canonical pathway-20 burden and pathway mutation-type composition candidate (50 columns, deduplicated against the base feature matrix) are all held fixed and unchanged. Target, test distribution, and Public LB do not define or select the gene groups or their split.",
